<BaseLayout title="About — Fernando Abad López" lang="en">
  <h1>About</h1>

  <p class="mt-8">
    I work on real-time simulation systems and 3D graphics. My territory is GPU shader programming,
    position-based physics simulation (PBD, XPBD), kinematic system validation, and everything that
    happens between the CPU and the graphics pipeline. I currently develop industrial simulation
    systems within a digital twin environment.
  </p>

  <p>
    I came to engineering the long way. I studied a higher vocational degree in Business
    Administration and Finance, and it was in advanced office software that the question that
    changed everything appeared: how does the thing inside a computer that makes it execute
    something actually work. I moved to Valencia to study Multimedia Engineering and specialized in
    GPU shaders, physics simulation, and algorithm validation against real data. My final degree
    project, in collaboration with the Instituto de Biomecánica de Valencia, was awarded Distinction
    (<em>Matrícula de Honor</em>).
  </p>

  <p>
    I'm looking for international remote positions or relocation within the EU, in technical teams
    working on simulation, real-time graphics, or adjacent systems.
  </p>

